{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/953019-how-long-do-indefinite-spells-usually-last","id":953019,"title":"How long do Indefinite Spells usually last?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-18T00:23:02-07:00","id":953019,"title":"How long do Indefinite Spells usually last?","content":"Indefinite spells keep going until they're either cancelled or broken in some way. If you have an important Indefinite spell you want to keep going (say you finally managed to make a magical servitor via a combination of two or more rank 5 arcana and you really don't want them to suffer a sudden existence failure just because your spell turned off) do you really need to worry about someone else dispelling it? If so, can you ward the spell so it's harder to break and, if so, how? <br /> <br /> Do you need to worry about the spell breaking down over time if Sleepers see something obviously supernatural, like a manservant made from stone? If the effect isn't obvious, like, even if you do a miracle by which you turn a hamster into a gerbil, the end result is a normal looking gerbil, does that risk breaking down by disbelief or anything? (Mage the Ascension had this come up and I haven't absorbed all of Awakening 2e's rules yet, so I wanted to ask.)<br /> <br /> Is it possible to do something and make the spell Lasting, even if that isn't given as a Reach option? Like by adding in Prime 5 or accepting a +3 Reach or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T00:37:37-07:00","id":953024,"title":"","content":"Protecting a spell from being dispelled is listed under Clash of Wills. You can spend Willpower to prevent a spell from being dispelled. Furthermore, Indefinite spells get a +4 bonus vs dispellation. Advanced Potency gives another bonus vs dispellation, but the book can't decide what it is. Some places it says +1 and some +2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-18-2016, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:16:28-07:00","id":953032,"title":"","content":"Dispelling is not Clash of Wills anywhere that I can see. It's a Prime 1 spell. And the bonus for Indefinite spells is just for Clash of Wills as far as I've found.<br /> <br /> But yes, you can give Advanced Potency.<br /> <br /> Prime gets a few defensive spells to protect further: Supernal Veil (Prime 2) can require a Clash of Wills to even see the spell to target it. Wards and Signs (Prime 2) can use its Potency as the Withstand for whatever it's cast on to resist spells, though with Arcana 5 like you were mentioning, your spell already has a Withstand of 5 to resist being dispelled (plus two for Advanced Potency), so it'd be pretty hard to improve upon that, but you could.<br /> <br /> Those are the methods I've found so far, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:32:16-07:00","id":953037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/953019-how-long-do-indefinite-spells-usually-last?p=953032#post953032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dispelling is not Clash of Wills anywhere that I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. I think I'm mixing this up with 1st edition rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:42:08-07:00","id":953044,"title":"","content":"To answer the rest of the question, if the results of your spell wouldn't trigger Quiessence then it won't deteriorate in the presence of Sleepers. If the spell doesn't have a Reach effect to make it Lasting it can't be, unless you persuade your ST. That being said, Indefinite could potentially last till the heat death of the universe so Lasting isn't really necessary. Even if it was Lasting at the very least some Mage could come along and destroy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T09:42:03-07:00","id":953890,"title":"","content":"Best way to protect a spell from dispellation is to cast a Wards and Signs on it, and then hide both of the spells with a Prime Veiling spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T22:08:29-07:00","id":954213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/953019-how-long-do-indefinite-spells-usually-last?p=953890#post953890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Best way to protect a spell from dispellation is to cast a Wards and Signs on it, and then hide both of the spells with a Prime Veiling spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or combine cast Wards and Signs and a veiling such that they both target the desired spell, themselves, and each other. That way they can't even dispel the veil and reveal it to other mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T00:57:58-07:00","id":954263,"title":"","content":"Can you cast on a spell that doesn't exist yet? That doesn't seem quite right...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:07:51-07:00","id":954266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/953019-how-long-do-indefinite-spells-usually-last?p=954263#post954263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you cast on a spell that doesn't exist yet? That doesn't seem quite right...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that a spell can target itself and that combined spells can target other spells in the combined casting, because their imagos are intertwined and are made together and can thus incorporate each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:14:56-07:00","id":955066,"title":"","content":"I would assume that a spell designed to hide something is itself hidden, otherwise it's kind of pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:19:14-07:00","id":955072,"title":"","content":"If such a capability worries you, throw a Reach on it and see if that trade-off is too high for your players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}